------------------------------------------------------------------------
What warnings does critTer generate on symtablelist.c, and what are your
disagreements with them? Copy the critTer warnings here, and express
your disagreement after each warning. If there are no warnings, then
write "None."

   symtablelist.c: line 77: medium priority:
   Do you want to validate 'pvValue' through an assert?

   symtablelist.c: line 108: medium priority:
   Do you want to validate 'pvExtra' through an assert?

   symtablelist.c: line 136: medium priority:
   Do you want to validate 'pvValue' through an assert?

   We shouldn't need to validate pvValue and pvExtra since they can be NULL, so non-NULL assertions would incorrectly reject these perfectly valid calls. 

------------------------------------------------------------------------
What warnings does splint generate on symtablehash.c, and what are your
disagreements with them? Copy the splint warnings here, and express your
disagreement after each warning. If there are no warnings, then write
"None."

Splint error: symtablehash.c: (in function SymTable_put)
symtablehash.c:323:17: Value oSymTable->buckets[] used before definition
An rvalue is used that may not be initialized to a value on some execution
path. (Use -usedef to inhibit warning)

Every bucket in the new bucket array is already initialized to NULL 
before the rehashing. Then Symtable_hash function returns an index 
within this array's bounds, so the bucket is already initialized 
before it is read.

